    "There is no useful numerical scalar check for this manifest-only change. Packaging-tool behavior requires a build rather than arithmetic emulation."
  ],
  "links": [],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "packaging",
      "title": "Carry native sources into JIT installations",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "MANIFEST.in retains include exllamav3/util/hadamard_data/* and adds recursive-include exllamav3/exllamav3_ext *. The wildcard covers the native tree rather than only compilation units, including nested headers and sources.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_2e97a9b795d44e759ffce867adc739d1", "call_8573483ce98740dfb8177c4e61d5ecaa"]
        },
        {
          "text": "setup.py enables include_package_data and disables precompilation when EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE is present. Its CUDAExtension configuration exists only when precompilation is enabled and Torch is available; otherwise setup_kwargs is empty.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_22b87af931524305a470773eb29d3224"]
        },
        {
          "text": "At runtime, ext.py first imports exllamav3_ext. On ModuleNotFoundError it recursively discovers .c, .cpp and .cu files beneath the installed Python module's exllamav3_ext directory, then passes them to torch.utils.cpp_extension.load with that directory as an include path.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_6ea8983b5e3449119ea9c0a353fc4b8b"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The broad recursive rule preserves both translation units and supporting headers without maintaining a second extension-specific file list. Its tradeoff is including the whole native subtree rather than narrowly selecting build inputs. Precompilation remains the existing alternative; neither build path's implementation changes.",
          "basis": "inference",
          "evidence": ["call_2e97a9b795d44e759ffce867adc739d1", "call_8573483ce98740dfb8177c4e61d5ecaa", "call_22b87af931524305a470773eb29d3224", "call_6ea8983b5e3449119ea9c0a353fc4b8b"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Explicitly includes the native extension tree in the package manifest so JIT installations can retain sources and headers needed by the runtime loader."
